# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) to make the LIVE opencode e2e reproducible on this machine.
# vitest.setup.ts loads .env.local before any test; shell vars override these (shell-WINS).
#
# These ONLY configure the live e2e suite (src/host/rc/opencode/driver.e2e.test.ts). With none set it
# targets a local `opencode serve` on the default port + the default model (Bedrock Claude Sonnet), and
# SKIPS when the server is unreachable — so unit tests and CI stay green with no setup.

# The opencode server the e2e attaches to (default http://127.0.0.1:4096). Left commented so a verbatim
# `cp .env.example .env.local` keeps the documented zero-config default; uncomment to point elsewhere.
# OPENCODE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4096

# The model the e2e drives, as "providerID/modelID". The default is Bedrock Claude Sonnet via the
# region-agnostic `global.` inference profile — a reliable tool-caller, so the tool + permission
# round-trips assert hard (no flaky tiny-model fallback, no self-skip). Override only to drive a
# different tool-capable model:
#   RC_OPENCODE_E2E_MODEL=amazon-bedrock/global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6
# The PROVIDER must be configured + authenticated on the opencode SERVER process itself, NOT here — for
# Bedrock the server needs the `amazon-bedrock` provider + AWS credentials in ITS environment. opencode's
# AI-SDK Bedrock client does NOT walk the IMDS instance-role chain (1.17.5), so export STATIC creds before
# launching it (`eval "$(aws configure export-credentials --format env)"`) or set AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK.
# The `global.` profile is region-agnostic, so any AWS_REGION works (there is no "right" region to pick).
# These test vars never reach the server; they only tell the e2e which server/model to drive.

# Per-live-turn budget in ms for a slow/contended box (default 120000). A STRUCTURAL turn that exceeds it
# SKIPS (never fails) — environmental slowness is not a code bug. The model-bearing scenarios (c) tool-use
# and (k) permission round-trip do NOT skip — they HARD assert within this budget, so a real regression
# goes red rather than silently skipping.
# RC_OPENCODE_E2E_TURN_MS=120000
